The great sage replied - Undoubtedly, I am desirous of marriage, and your daughter has neither
married anyone, nor has she given her word to anyone else. Therefore, according to the Vedic method,
we both can get married. Meaning: Before accepting the daughter of Swyambhuva Manu, in front of Kardama Muni,
there were many things to consider. Firstly, Devahuti had decided to marry him. She did not want to make any other man her husband.
This was the biggest
considerable thing, because when a woman, at the very first glance, offers her heart to a man,
it is difficult to take it back. This is the psychology of Siyo ©. Also,
before this, she was not married; she was a weaver. From all these things, Kardam Muni
accepted him. Therefore, he said, "Yes, according to the religious rules of marriage, I
accept your daughter."" Marriage has many forms. The best marriage is one in which, after calling the suitable groom, the bride is adorned with JG and ornaments, and according to the father's ability,
a dowry is given, and the bride is offered. There are other types of marriage as well, such as Gandharva.
Marriage and love marriage. These are also considered marriage. If a girl forcefully goes to Hari and
later accepts her as wife, then that is also considered marriage.
But Kardam Muni
Accepted the best system of marriage, because the girl's father wanted and that girl
was also worthy off. He had not loved anyone else. From all these things, Kardam Muni
became agreeable to accepting the daughter of Swayambhuva Manu.
